{
  "version": "1.0",
  "_comment": "STING standard panel schedule templates (ISO 19650 identification + BS 7671 circuit data). 'Panel templates → Create / update' builds one Revit PanelScheduleTemplate per entry with PanelScheduleTemplate.Create and SetTableData, and rebuilds it in place on re-run. Template NAMES must match the templateName values in STING_PANEL_SCHEDULE_TEMPLATES.json so the board→template rules resolve to them. A project can override or add templates (merged by name) in <project>/_BIM_COORD/panel_schedule_specs.json.",
  "_paramSyntax": "'bip:NAME' = Revit BuiltInParameter; anything else = a STING shared parameter (must be bound — run Load Params). Header and footer cells read Electrical Equipment (the board); body cells read Electrical Circuits. 'category': 'ProjectInformation' asks for a project parameter — Revit may refuse it in a panel schedule, in which case the build reports it.",
  "_columnsNote": "Only parameters that something actually writes are used. Zs, CPC size and the BS 7671 adiabatic result are NOT columns: no command writes them onto circuits yet, and an always-empty column misleads more than a missing one.",
  "templates": [
    {
      "name": "STING - 3-Phase Distribution Board",
